'''Nala Se's private lab''' was a secret research [[laboratory]] used by [[Kaminoan]] [[Chief Medical Scientist]] [[Nala Se]] before and during the [[Clone Wars]]. Situated beneath [[Tipoca City]], the laboratory's existence was known to only a few, and it had a private entrance to [[Kamino]]'s [[Kamino tube system|tube system]]. Nala Se created the unaltered [[Cloning|clone]] [[Omega]] in the lab, as well as enhancing the [[gene]]tic mutations of the original members of [[Clone Force 99]] there. Early in the [[Imperial Era]], Omega, [[Tech]], [[Echo]], and [[Wrecker]] used the lab as a backdoor entrance to Tipoca [[City]] while trying to [[Rescue of Hunter|rescue]] the "Bad Batch's" leader, [[Hunter]]. The Batch later retreated to the lab after the Empire [[Attack on Kamino|destroyed]] Tipoca City, using the lab's medical tubes as makeshift capsules to reach the surface of the ocean.

==Description==
[[Nala Se]]'s private [[Laboratory|lab]] was located deep [[Water|underwater]], connected to the lower levels of [[Tipoca City]], the [[capital]] of [[Kamino]], a [[planet]]<ref name="Return to Kamino" /> [[extragalactic]] of [[the galaxy]] proper.<ref name="SWCL">[[Star Wars: Complete Locations (2016)|''Star Wars: Complete Locations'']]</ref> An isolated structure on the [[ocean]] floor, the lab was equipped with medical tubes and multiple [[computer]]s.<ref name="Kamino Lost">{{TBB|Kamino Lost}}</ref> It could be accessed by taking a private entrance to the [[Kamino tube system]] from a [[secret landing platform]] outside the [[city]] proper, as well as from within the city itself.<ref name="Return to Kamino" />

==History==
{{Quote|When the clone has returned, confine her to the sublevel facility. Once you have retrieved the genetic material needed, terminate her.|[[Lama Su]] ordering Nala Se|<ref name="Bounty Lost">{{TBB|Bounty Lost}}</ref>}}
The private research lab used by [[Kaminoan]] [[Chief Medical Scientist]] Nala Se was in use during her creation of the [[clone trooper]]s of the [[Grand Army of the Republic]], with only a few people aware of its existence. She created the unique unaltered [[Gender|female]] [[Cloning|clone]] [[Omega]] in the lab,<ref name="Return to Kamino" /> one of the only two clones—the other being [[Boba Fett|Boba]]—created who lacked the age acceleration and obedience modifications of the standard clone troopers.<ref name="Bounty Lost">{{TBB|Bounty Lost}}</ref> Later, Nala Se enhanced the [[gene]]tic mutations of four clones who were designated as [[Clone Force 99|Experimental Unit 99]] in the lab, which was witnessed by Omega. The four clones only stayed in the lab for a short [[time]] before they were sent back to be with the rest of the clones.<ref name="Return to Kamino" />

In [[19 BBY]],<ref name="Date">"[[Return to Kamino]]" takes place shortly after the formation of the [[Galactic Empire]], which ''[[Star Wars: Galactic Atlas]]'' dates to [[19 BBY]].</ref> Kamino was taken over by the newly-established [[Galactic Empire]]. Around this time, Nala Se planned to retrieve genetic material from Omega,<ref name="Bounty Lost" /> but Omega ended up fleeing the planet with the Bad Batch as the Empire began their takeover.<ref name="Aftermath">{{TBB|Aftermath (episode)}}</ref> As part of an Imperial [[Attack on Kamino|operation]] to strip Kamino of all useful personnel, clones, and technology,<ref name="Return to Kamino" /> Nala Se was taken into custody on the orders of [[Vice Admiral]] [[Edmon Rampart|Rampart]] after she was discovered to have been gathering medical personnel in an attempt to flee the planet<ref name="War-Mantle">{{TBB|War-Mantle}}</ref>. Afterwards, as newly-introduced recruited [[Stormtrooper|TK troopers]] began rounding up medical personnel onto [[transport]]s, [[Death|killing]] any who resisted, and deactivating [[droid]]s, the [[medical droid]] [[AZI-345211896246498721347|AZI-3]] managed to escape, hiding in Nala Se's lab, which was by that time empty and devoid of experiments.<ref name="Return to Kamino" />

Later, several clones from Unit 99&mdash;original members [[Tech]] and [[Wrecker]], as well as later recruit [[Echo]]&mdash;entered Tipoca City via the lab's secret entrance at Omega's suggestion, hoping to [[Rescue of Hunter|rescue]] [[squad]] leader [[Hunter]] from the Empire. Arriving via the tube system, Wrecker commented that the lab looked just like every other Kaminoan lab he had ever seen. Omega explained that she had been created there, and that was also where the so-called "Bad Batch" had begun. When Wrecker asked if that was true, Tech pointedly inquired how he was supposed to know that. Omega reminisced that the squad's mutations had been enhanced there before they were sent back to be with the others, but the conversation was interrupted when Echo discovered that Tipoca City's [[computer]]s had been wiped. As the Batch was discussing why this had happened, the group was startled by AZI-3, who filled them in on the recent goings-on. Tech then detected Hunter's [[comlink]] pinging from the central cloning platform, and Omega led the way out of the lab with AZI-3 as they headed to the upper city.<ref name="Return to Kamino" />

During a confrontation in the city, the Batch rescued Hunter and captured their former member [[Crosshair]], who had remained with the Empire. However, the Empire began to destroy Tipoca City with the clones still trapped inside.<ref name="Return to Kamino" /> The section of the city they were trapped in sank and landed on top of a mostly-intact tube leading back to the lab, so at Omega's suggestion they cut their way into the tube and used it as an exit. Near the entrance to the lab, a [[kamoradon sea dragon]] attempted to attack the group, but AZI-3 was able to use the last of the facility's power to drive it off before they entered the lab. Once there, Hunter asked what the facility was, and Tech told him and Crosshair what Omega had earlier said about the facility's purpose and their past there. Omega discovered, however, that the tube leading from the lab back to the landing platform had been broken, leaving them stranded.<ref name="Kamino Lost" />

==Behind the scenes==
Nala Se's private lab first appeared in "[[Return to Kamino]]," the fifteenth episode of the [[The Bad Batch Season 1|first season]] of ''[[Star Wars: The Bad Batch]]''.<ref name="Return to Kamino" /> It was first identified in an entry on the official [[Databank (2014-)|Databank]], although the entry was illustrated with a picture of the [[Tipoca City Training Facility]] storage room instead of the actual lab.<ref name="DB">{{Databank|nala-se-s-private-lab|Nala Se's private lab}}</ref>

